<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - February statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - February statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in February 1997 and consumption, imports and exports in January/February compared with 1996 were as follows, said the Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p>    METAL		    PRODUCTION (FEB)   CONSUMPTION (JAN/FEB)</p>
<p>		    1997	 1996	    1997	 1996</p>
<p> Aluminium	   91,000     95,100	  75,330     55,772</p>
<p> Lead			 0	    0	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Copper		14,446     14,166	  45,529     31,256</p>
<p> Tin		    1,364	1,395	     485	  994</p>
<p> Magnesium		n/a	  n/a	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,300	1,068	  (1,441)	 196</p>
<p> Zinc		  13,334     12,776	  22,602     12,834</p>
<p> METAL		  EXPORTS (JAN/FEB)	 IMPORTS (JAN/FEB)</p>
<p>		    1997	 1996	    1997	 1996</p>
<p> Aluminium	  133,697    160,964	  23,447     18,424</p>
<p> Lead			15	   13	   4,936	  786</p>
<p> Copper		 5,095	9,549	  25,733     22,648</p>
<p> Tin		    2,508	1,829		10	    0</p>
<p> Magnesium		 82	  765	   1,197	  299</p>
<p> Nickel		   752	  931	   1,250	1,311</p>
<p> Zinc		   6,484     17,492	     376	1,728</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
